            <ArticleTitle>Women's health issues and nuclear medicine, Part I: Women and heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>89-92; quiz 103, 105</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is the first article of a four-part series on women's health issues and nuclear medicine. This article will review women and heart disease. After reading this article the technologist will be able to: (a) compare and contrast the differences in diagnosing coronary artery disease between men and women; (b) explain the importance of radionuclide myocardial perfusion imaging in diagnosing and stratifying risk of coronary artery disease in women; and (c) list and explain the technical challenges of imaging women's hearts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
